okbook:Garlic|garlic]], minced\n* 2 red [[Cookbook:Chilli|chillies]], cut into 1 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]] pieces\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] minced [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Horseradish|horseradish]], cut into matchsticks\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Scallion|scallions]], cut into 1 cm pieces\n* 500 g cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 25 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Barbecue Sauce|barbeque sauce]]\n* 2 tbsp black [[Cookbook:Soy sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 1½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n\n=== Toppings (optional) ===\n* Fried egg\n* Pickles\n* [[Cookbook:Tomato|Tomato]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cucumber|Cucumber]]\n* Fried onion\n* Salt\n* Shrimp crackers\n* [[Cookbook:Beef|Beef]] steak\n* Vegetables like [[Cookbook:Corn|corn]], [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]], and [[Cookbook:Pea|peas]]\n\n== Equipment ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|Frying pan]]\n* [[Cookbook:Knife|Knife]]\n* [[Cookbook:Stovetop|Stove]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Heat the olive oil and sesame oil in a non-stick pan. Fry the garlic and red onion until fragrant. Stir until the garlic and red onion are golden brown. \n# Add the red chilli and pork. Stir until the pork changes color.\n# Add horseradish, scallion, rice, barbecue sauce, black soy sauce, salt, and pepper. Stir until well-mixed.\n# Serve with toppings as desired.\n\n[[Category:Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fried rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using barbecue sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using horseradish]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Barbecue Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Heat the olive oil and sesame oil in a non-stick pan. Fry the garlic and red onion until fragrant. Stir until the garlic and red onion are golden brown.","sourceText":"Heat the olive oil and sesame oil in a non-stick pan. Fry the garlic and red onion until fragrant. Stir until the garlic and red onion are golden brown.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add the red chilli and pork. Stir until the pork changes color.","sourceText":"Add the red chilli and pork. Stir until the pork changes color.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Add horseradish, scallion, rice, barbecue sauce, black soy sauce, salt, and pepper. Stir until well-mixed.","sourceText":"Add horseradish, scallion, rice, barbecue sauce, black soy sauce, salt, and pepper. Stir until well-mixed.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Serve with toppings as desired.","sourceText":"Serve with toppings as desired.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:201861","recordId":"wikibooks-201861-r4517677","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4517677","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Barbecue%20Fried%20Rice&oldid=4517677","sourceSha256":"1fb5bea842043c7b7a2f0239799df5cd99c44602746a20562eb48b1b086d4769","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by l